# `die` declared in `package main`. Both the warning and the error are pinned,
# because it is the PAIR that was wrong: the warning used to offer "call it
# qualified as `pkg.die(...)`" and the very next line makes the declaration a
# hard error, so that remedy cannot be taken. There is no package prefix in main
# -- pkg_mangle is the identity there -- so the name is simply taken. The same
# declaration in a LIBRARY package is accepted and the qualified call really
# works, which is why the other wording is still right there
# (tests/warn/shadow_builtin.ty). Found writing tools/tycho-diff.
fn die(m: string) -> int:
    return 1

fn main():
    println("x")
